source.description:
The class diagram text in this grammar, up to 100,000 characters. One item per line. Classes: "class Name {", "interface Name {", "abstract class Name {" or "enum Name {", then one member per line, then "}" on its own line ("class Name" alone declares an empty class; a stereotype may follow the name, e.g. "class Name <<entity>> {"). Fields: "+name: Type". Methods: "+name(arg: Type, other: Type): ReturnType". Visibility + public, - private, # protected, ~ package (optional). "{static}" or "{abstract}" before the name marks static or abstract members. Enum constants: one NAME per line. Relations: "Animal <|-- Dog" (inheritance), "Shape <|.. Circle" (realization), "Car *-- Wheel" (composition), "Team o-- Player" (aggregation), "Customer --> Order" (association), "Report ..> Printer" (dependency), "A -- B" (link); arrows may point either way (Dog --|> Animal). Optional multiplicities in quotes next to each class and a label after a colon: Customer "1" --> "0..*" Order : places. "%%" starts a comment line. Example: "class Customer {
+name: String
+orders(): List<Order>
}
class Order {
-total: Decimal
}
Customer "1" --> "*" Order : places".
